  "interpretation": [
    "With kidney markers the label is almost deterministic (creatinine, albumin and specific gravity define the diagnosis), so ~0.99+ AUROC reflects label construction, not clinical foresight.",
    "Without kidney markers, routine data (hemoglobin, PCV, hypertension, diabetes, appetite, oedema) still separate CKD well; this is the payer use case of flagging likely-undiagnosed CKD for testing.",
    "Neither result is a deterioration (progression) model: that needs longitudinal labs, which is why PredictMed's main track uses the time-series payer cohort and the digital twin."
  ]
